  "query_preview": "..\nToday into Sunday night: Satellite observations continue to \nexhibit a persistant low stratus deck that lingers through most of\nthe weekend. This deck will slowly lift precluding any fog across\nthe region for tonight. \n\nContinued NWP guidance has consistently similar messaging through\nthe weekend - A trough running from the Hudson Bay into Montana \nwill bring colder than normal temps through Sunday night and \nisolated snow showers through Saturday night. Wind chills this \nweekend through Tuesday are expected to be in the teens to single \ndigits during the AM hours. Coldest wind chills will be around 6-8\nAM.\n\nMonday to Wednesday night: Northwest flow will gradually \ntransition to a ridge with chinook arch. Expect a slow warming \ntrend with dry conditions and developing overcast high clouds. \n\nThursday onward: Ensembles disagree on how to break down the \nridge with mainly a weak trough to zonal flow. But, some lesser \nmembers are producing a near persistent ridge. Effectively, the \nforecast from this point onward becomes low confidence with the \nfull expectation of it changing in the next forecast cycle. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\n- High confidence(60-90%) through Monday night \n\n- Moderate confidence(40-60%) in the forecast from Tuesday to \n  Wednesday night.\n\n- Low confidence(15-25%) Thrusday onward.  \n\nFINDLEY/GAH",
